I don't think anyone involved with nethack is "lazy" - it's all
voluntary and for fun after all.  But I think the main nethack project
and perhaps other subprojects would benefit from better coordination
and organization.  If information overload is stifling you, it could
be that way and worse for the devteam.  Hence my exhortations to get
nethack related projects under one umbrella as much as possible, and
make it visible so that everyone knows what's going on and work isn't
duplicated.  The overall goal is to get bugfixes and nifty new
well-balanced code released on a better basis that once every 3 years.
Even once a year would be fantastic in my book.

